	(text "MOTOR SWITCH (record section 4). TPS48111 datasheet Figure 9-14 topology:\n  back-to-back N-FETs, common source, pre-charge through Q403 and Q402's body\n  diode.\nOpen = open both ways: back-drive never reaches the board, so the regen shunt\n  sizes for the powered 6.8 W case.  FETs Q401/Q402: 100 V (58.6 V back-EMF),\n  D2PAK class; TODO pick part.\nR401 2 mOhm: 30 mV at 15 A. OC R404 39.2k = 15.2 A for 10 ms (C402 680n, R405\n  100k = LATCH-OFF; firmware re-arms by toggling MOTOR_EN). SC R403 3.4k = 30\n  A in 1.2 us.\nIMON R406 8.25k: 3.0 V at 20 A into an ADC1 pin.  CBST C401 470n.  UVLO\n  R407/R408 470k/24.9k: on above ~23 V.  Q404 sits beside Q401/Q402 in layout:\n  150 C cutoff.\nMOTOR_EN floats during P4 boot: R409 pulldown + internal pulldown = off.\n  INA_ALERT_N (open drain) pulls EN low: INA228 limits cut the motor with no\n  MCU.\nPRE-CHARGE: drive input measured 150 uF (hw-x65). PRECHARGE_EN high ~75 ms\n  (R412 100R, 0.36 A peak, ~0.1 J), then MOTOR_EN high, then PRECHARGE_EN low.\nD401 SMBJ48CA: stands off above the 45 V clamp, clamps under the 100 V FETs;\n  catches the hot-plug ring of the drive's ceramic input."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
